  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Carahsoft Technology obligated $1.9B in FY2026 to date across 1,999 awards, with an average award size of $936K and year-over-year change up 3.4%. Carahsoft Technology obligations rose from $1.2B in FY21 to $1.9B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer and obligated $912M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $248M and the Department of Homeland Security at $180M. Software Publishers is the dominant market with $1.3B and an additional Software Publishers entry at $168M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $289M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $114M. Carahsoft Technology also shows obligations in Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $25.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $11.5M, plus smaller markets at $2.7M, $290K, $288K, and $231K. Carahsoft Technology current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations. Carahsoft Technology figures in this report are contract obligations except where table notes identify award-value figures as total contract values.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of Carahsoft Technology in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer and obligated $912M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $248M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $180M. The Department of Agriculture obligated $110M and the General Services Administration obligated $86.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets drive Carahsoft Technology obligations?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the largest market with entries at $1.3B and $168M. Other Computer Related Services accounts for $289M and Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $114M. Carahsoft Technology also records obligations in Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $25.4M and R&D in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $11.5M, plus smaller markets at $2.7M, $290K, $288K, and $231K."
      }
    ]
  },
